<rss xmlns:content="http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:jrdate="https://fengziclassmate.github.io/journal-rss/ns/dates/1" xmlns:ns2="http://prismstandard.org/namespaces/basic/2.0/" xmlns:ns3="https://fengziclassmate.github.io/journal-rss/ns/unified/1" version="2.0"><channel><title>Nature Communications</title><link>https://www.nature.com/ncomms.rss</link><description>Publisher feed and retained journal history.</description><item><title>Brønsted/Lewis acid-catalyzed divergent cascade cyclization of alkoxyallene for the total synthesis of eburnane and aspidofractinine alkaloids</title>
            <link>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-026-79505-6</link>
            <content:encoded>
                &lt;p&gt;Nature Communications, Published online: 16 November 2026; &lt;a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-026-79505-6"&gt;doi:10.1038/s41467-026-79505-6&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;Eburnane and aspidofractinine alkaloids are biogenetically related yet structurally distinct polycyclic monoterpenoids, whose syntheses have traditionally proceeded separately. Here, the authors report a divergent cascade from a common alkoxyallene precursor, enabling access to both scaffolds through acid controlled tandem pathways and total syntheses of representative alkaloids.</content:encoded>
            <dc:title>Brønsted/Lewis acid-catalyzed divergent cascade cyclization of alkoxyallene for the total synthesis of eburnane and aspidofractinine alkaloids</dc:title>
            <dc:creator>Fengchi Hu</dc:creator><dc:creator>Qiude Huang</dc:creator><dc:creator>Su Su Htwe Chaw</dc:creator><dc:creator>Chengfeng Xia</dc:creator>
