            <link>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-026-79078-4</link>
            <content:encoded>
                &lt;p&gt;Nature Communications, Published online: 16 November 2026; &lt;a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-026-79078-4"&gt;doi:10.1038/s41467-026-79078-4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;A physics-informed neural network embeds coking and heat transfer knowledge via an output integration layer and region-weighted loss to predict reactor spatiotemporal fields; it matches conventional simulation results, improves peak wall temperature accuracy, and runs about five orders of magnitude faster than conventional simulations.</content:encoded>
            <dc:title>Knowledge-guided machine learning deciphers spatiotemporal dynamics in chemical reactor systems</dc:title>
